ulture. CEO compensation is 21\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["CAVA Group, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $5.7B market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +27% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 25% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $26M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.90\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 332% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":3.322622123294137},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $5.3M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-5288874.03},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 12% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 5% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Does CAVA\u2019s (NYSE:CAVA) Midwest Expansion Mean For Its Growth Story?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/growth/what-does-cavas-nysecava-midwest-expansion-mean-for-its-growth-story","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795200840.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.677,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Dutch Bros vs. CAVA: Revenue Trends May Be Misleading. Here's What Else to Watch.","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/dutch-